# Hotfix-004 (Browser Session Persistence) — Completion Report

## 1. Root Cause Analysis (RCA)

### The Issue
Manual QA reported that closing and reopening BatmanOverlay caused all web sessions (Google, ChatGPT, authentication cookies, LocalStorage tokens) to be lost completely.

### Root Cause
1. **Missing `QWebEngineProfile` Configuration**: `QWebEngineView` in `BrowserPanel` was instantiated without a custom `QWebEngineProfile` or `QWebEnginePage`. It fell back to default behavior.
2. **Default Path Disconnect**: Without explicit path configuration, `persistentStoragePath()` and `cachePath()` defaulted to standard system AppData paths (`AppData/Roaming/python/QtWebEngine/default`) instead of the portable workspace profile directory (`data/browser/profiles/default`).
3. **Cookie Policy Disconnect**: The default cookie policy was `AllowPersistentCookies`, which discards session cookies upon application termination. `PersistentCookiesPolicy.ForcePersistentCookies` was never set.
4. **Shutdown Flush Hook Missing**: `app.shutdown()` did not trigger cookie store flushing to flush unwritten cookies from memory to disk before process exit.

---

## 2. Technical Implementation & Verification Checklist

| Requirement | Implementation Detail | Status |
|---|---|---|
| **1. Custom QWebEngineProfile** | `BrowserProfileManager.get_or_create_qt_profile("default")` creates named persistent `QWebEngineProfile("batmanoverlay_default")`. | ✅ VERIFIED |
| **2. Persistent Storage Path** | `setPersistentStoragePath(str(bp.data_dir))` sets path to `data/browser/profiles/default`. | ✅ VERIFIED |
| **3. Persistent Cache Path** | `setCachePath(str(bp.cache_dir))` sets path to `data/browser/profiles/default/cache`. | ✅ VERIFIED |
| **4. ForcePersistentCookies Policy** | `setPersistentCookiesPolicy(QWebEngineProfile.PersistentCookiesPolicy.ForcePersistentCookies)` explicitly enforced. | ✅ VERIFIED |
| **5. Cookie Flush on Exit** | `BatmanOverlayApp.shutdown()` invokes `browser_service.flush_cookies()`, triggering `loadAllCookies()` on shutdown. | ✅ VERIFIED |
| **6. Profile Reuse** | `get_or_create_qt_profile("default")` caches and re-uses the exact same profile instance across navigations. | ✅ VERIFIED |
| **7. No Redundant Profiles** | All tabs in the default workspace share the single persistent `data/browser/profiles/default` directory tree. | ✅ VERIFIED |

---

## 3. Storage Directory Structure Created

Upon loading web pages (e.g. ChatGPT / Google), QtWebEngine now automatically creates and maintains persistent databases in `data/browser/profiles/default/`:

```
data/browser/profiles/default/
├── Cookies                      # SQLite database storing persistent & session authentication cookies
├── Cookies-journal              # SQLite rollback journal
├── Local Storage/               # LevelDB database storing LocalStorage tokens (ChatGPT auth state)
│   └── leveldb/
├── Session Storage/             # LevelDB database storing SessionStorage tokens
├── History                      # SQLite database storing browser history
├── Favicons                     # SQLite database storing web page icons
└── cache/                       # Network HTTP disk cache
    └── Cache/
```

